ation/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"a73ed322041008e164cc1bf0f466c254b35991dcaa5e32b2648fc952c8f43fb9","event_uuid":"489f255e-7fa3-4d39-aa6c-e69064e5098e","position":{"commit_sha":"a0accfc49e1b388e06376db3590e7dfe723aad4b","position":"1795427118615044001-489f255e-7fa3-4d39-aa6c-e69064e5098e"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Plan review 2026-11-22 22:03 PST (sandboxed, api.anthropic.com allowed): BLOCK on G1G2 - infra/gerrit/service-user.sh (the token create/rotate tool) puts the token in ssh/aws/awk argv and was not classified. Response: survey and split written into the description. This ticket keeps the production review-bot fix (src/rebar); operator tooling, the workflow and the docs moved to immoral-heated-doctorfish (filed, discovered_from), which also owns service-user.sh. The rotation decision should follow doctorfish's service-user.sh fix. Acceptance criteria unchanged. Separately, the first sandboxed review at 21:44 was INDETERMINATE because that command did not list api.anthropic.com for the sandbox proxy (sub-exceptions: httpx.ProxyError 403 'not in allowed_domains'); the classifier called it a transient blip - filed vinyl-dubnium-squamata.","timestamp":1795413964157095001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented in commit 5d66f7a6f04 (worktree bug-7279-cred-argv, from gerrit main c924c0ea2e8): fetch URL without userinfo; Basic header via URL-scoped http.<base>/.extraHeader in GIT_CONFIG_* env on the Gerrit fetch only, appended after inherited entries; GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0. New tests (8) fail 7/8 on the old code and pass on the fix. Live check 22:25 PST: clone_change_ref of change 3530 with this machine's Gerrit credential fetched the current revision; a ps sampler (332 samples, counts only) saw the Gerrit git fetch 35 times and the credential, its encodings, URL userinfo or extraHeader 0 times. make verify running before push.","timestamp":1795414961369352001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3532 patch set 1 (5d66f7a6f04): LLM-Review +1, Verified -1. Cause: test_the_header_is_scoped_to_gerrit_by_git_itself ran git config --get-urlmatch with cwd inside the CI checkout, where actions/checkout persists its own http.https://github.com/.extraheader, so the github.com lookup found the runner's header (rc 0, not 1). Test-isolation defect, not a product defect; the test printed no header value (failure line is only assert 0 == 1). Reproduced locally in a repo carrying a github.com extraheader (old test fails, fixed test passes). Fix: lookup runs outside any repo with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null, GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, GIT_CEILING_DIRECTORIES. Also addressed the LLM-Review advisory: test_clone_change_ref_timeout_does_not_leak_the_bot_token now injects a credential into the timed-out argv so the redaction path is still exercised. make verify on da065134e87 exit 0 (21848 passed / 34 skipped, 231 passed / 2 skipped). Pushed as patch set 2. Box baseline 23:12-23:24 PST on bot-deployed-sha c924c0ea2e8 (pre-fix), read-only SSM ps sampler printing counts only: 3096 samples, review-bot Gerrit fetch seen 13 times, URL userinfo in 13 of 13 - the check detects the leak.","timestamp":1795422217320908001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Change 3532 merged as 053604a2618 (patch set 2 da065134e87: LLM-Review +1, Verified +1, 0 unresolved, submitted 00:50 PST 2026-11-23). Autodeploy rolled the review-bot: bot-deployed-sha 053604a2618 and container restarted at 00:53 PST; /opt/rebar gerrit_client.py contains the new _gerrit_git_env. Box ps check after deploy is NOT yet proven: two read-only counts-only SSM sampling windows (00:54-01:19 and 01:19-01:44 PST, about 7150 samples each) saw no review-bot Gerrit fetch at all (positive control 0; no change was awaiting review), so their 0 userinfo / 0 header counts are vacuous. Pre-deploy baseline with the same sampler saw 13 fetches, 13 with userinfo. Remaining: run the same sampler during the next real review and expect gerrit_fetch_lines_seen >= 1 with userinfo_lines=0 and auth_header_lines=0. Token NOT rotated: the [non-codebase] rotation criterion is the operator's decision; doctorfish (immoral-heated-doctorfish) owns making service-user.sh, the rotation tool, keep the new token out of argv. Leaving this ticket in_progress.","timestamp":1795427118615044001}],"created_at":1795406642845884001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"cdb8441c-ff96-44ae-8bfc-45075ce395ff","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"585e-8f49-dff0-4ada"},{"link_uuid":"97381b8b-33a1-476e-92c9-0f69eecd7ca4","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"},{"link_uuid":"da1362b6-8354-444f-a529-0a9d978dd3f1","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ab24-3683-41bf-4172"},{"link_uuid":"d8eec347-12fe-42e4-9a7e-95a2e175bac9","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"a7b3-549d-a312-4316"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n`GerritClient.clone_change_ref` (src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py) builds a fetch URL whose userinfo part holds the bot user and `gerrit_bot_token` and passes it as a positional argument to `git fetch -q --depth 2`. The secret is therefore in the git process's command line for the length of the fetch. On 2026-11-22 at 19:32 PST a read-only `ps` sample on the prod host (taken for ultrashort-emaciated-krill) showed the full URL, password included, in the review-bot's git child. Anyone who can list processes on the host or in the container (`ps`, `/proc/<pid>/cmdline`, SSM command output, monitoring agents) can read it. The token is the review-bot account's dual-scope Gerrit credential (REST and git).\n\n## Survey and split\nSurvey of the credential-in-argv class (2026-11-22): in `src/rebar`, `clone_change_ref` is the only site that puts a credential in a subprocess argv or URL (the other authenticated paths send headers in-process via urllib/httpx, for example `GerritClient._request`, gerrit_client.py:78-95). The review-bot container's other git credential, the tickets PAT, already comes from an env-reading credential helper (infra/compose/Dockerfile.reviewbot:63-66). The remaining sites are operator-workstation tooling and docs: infra/gerrit/service-user.sh (the token create/rotate tool: ssh `--http-password`, `aws ssm put-parameter --value`, `awk -v`), infra/gerrit/{smoke-check,reviewbot-e2e,feature-branch-e2e,feature-branch-e2e-scenarios,feature-branch-inventory}.sh, .github/workflows/external-integration.yml:783,787, AGENTS.md:90 and CONTRIBUTING.md:268-270. Those are owned by immoral-heated-doctorfish (linked discovered_from), which extends this ticket's static guard to them. This ticket fixes the production review-bot leak so it can deploy first; the operator's rotation decision (the `[non-codebase]` item) should wait for doctorfish's service-user.sh fix so the new token is not exposed on the operator workstation.\n\n## Approach\nRoot cause: `clone_change_ref` (src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py:347-360) percent-encodes `bot_user:gerrit_bot_token` into the fetch URL's userinfo and passes the URL as a git argument.\n\nFix: build the fetch URL with no userinfo (`<gerrit_base_url>/a/<project>`; the box uses `http://gerrit:8080`, config.py:180). Hand git the bot's existing Basic value (`GerritClient._auth`, gerrit_client.py:74-76) as URL-scoped config `http.<gerrit_base_url>/.extraHeader = Authorization: Basic ...` through git's own `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT`/`GIT_CONFIG_KEY_<n>`/`GIT_CONFIG_VALUE_<n>` environment variables (git >= 2.31; the image is python:3.12-slim, Dockerfile.reviewbot:5, Debian git 2.39). The entry is appended after inherited entries: the container sets `GIT_CONFIG_COUNT=1` for `safe.directory` (docker-compose.yml:88-90). If an inherited count is not a number, git itself rejects every call, so the helper treats it as 0 and writes a valid count of 1. `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0` makes a rejected header fail fast. Only the Gerrit fetch child gets this environment; the GitHub tickets fetch keeps the inherited one, and the URL scope stops git sending the header to any other host. Checked on git 2.56: `git config --get-urlmatch http.extraheader` returns the value for the Gerrit URL and nothing for https://github.com/navapbc/rebar. A child's environment is readable only by its owner and root, not by `ps`. `_redact` stays on error paths.\n\nNo rebar config key, `REBAR_*` env var or flag (the mechanism ratchet censuses only `REBAR_*` env vars, scripts/_mechanism_delta/detect_config.py:83-95). This change performs no rotation.\n\n## Scope\n- src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py: userinfo-free fetch URL; auth header through `GIT_CONFIG_*` env on the Gerrit fetch only.\n- tests/unit/test_review_bot_git_credential_argv.py (new): the tests below.\n\n## Testing\n- Unit: drive `clone_change_ref` with a recording `subprocess.run`. No argv element of any call contains the raw token, the percent-encoded token, or the base64 `user:token`; the Gerrit fetch's env carries `http.<base>/.extraHeader` appended after an inherited `safe.directory` entry, plus `GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=0`; a non-numeric inherited count yields a count of 1; no other git call's env carries an Authorization value. Real `git config --get-urlmatch` against that env returns the header for the Gerrit URL and nothing for GitHub.\n- Static guard over `src/rebar/**/*.py`: no f-string or format URL puts a token/password/secret variable before `@` (the old shape), and no subprocess argv literal carries `extraHeader`/`Authorization`. Doctorfish extends it to shell surfaces.\n- Real path, locally: run `clone_change_ref` against the live Gerrit with this machine's Gerrit credential (from `git credential fill`, never printed) and confirm it fetches a real change ref. In parallel, a Python sampler reads `ps` output every 50 ms and counts, in-process (the secret never goes into a grep argv), (a) git fetch processes for the Gerrit URL (positive control, must be >= 1) and (b) command lines containing the credential, its encodings, `@` userinfo, or `extraHeader` (must be 0).\n- On the box after merge and autodeploy, during a real review: a read-only SSM loop samples `ps` until it sees a review-bot git fetch for `/a/rebar` (positive control >= 1), and counts command lines with URL userinfo (`://[^/ ]*:[^/ ]*@`), `extraHeader` or `Authorization` (must be 0). It prints counts only, never command lines.\n- `make verify` green; `python scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py --check` exits 0.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] No review-bot git invocation carries a credential in its argv; the fetch authenticates through a channel that is not in the command line (credential helper, or a header passed through the environment).\n- [ ] A test fails if `clone_change_ref` puts the bot token in the git argv.\n- [ ] [non-codebase] The review-bot Gerrit token is rotated after the fix deploys, since it has appeared in process listings.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/review_bot/gerrit_client.py","reason":"userinfo-free fetch URL; auth header via GIT_CONFIG_* env on the Gerrit fetch"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_review_bot_git_credential_argv.py","reason":"new guard tests: no credential in argv"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"],["relates_to","a7b3-549d-a312-4316"],["relates_to","ab24-3683-41bf-4172"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"e987d3aa-3ba4-42aa-8f96-526dcb92d1d5","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"7279-b619-cb42-40b8","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Review-bot passes its Gerrit HTTP password in git's argv, visible in any process listing","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["7dab1145-9937-4289-a839-d7c58c053422","0f142822-3248-41bf-9160-45e5baf7dfc5","97381b8b-33a1-476e-92c9-0f69eecd7ca4","8ea8e88c-a3a2-427c-b3ae-42ed2f2c51d8","ad421f84-71c7-44a0-b3be-eb8aeaa7cd6f","da6b305b-6b2d-48ea-8e38-bd75394982cf","c6dec38d-f840-476a-9193-4aa13d7c3c76","e987d3aa-3ba4-42aa-8f96-526dcb92d1d5","d48b3d6f-6284-479e-a2dc-770fd7249ce2","2394f12d-45f8-4a44-976f-12b67f3561de","da1362b6-8354-444f-a529-0a9d978dd3f1","16b66119-85a3-4374-942f-fa6fdd2aa3a8","d8eec347-12fe-42e4-9a7e-95a2e175bac9","489f255e-7fa3-4d39-aa6c-e69064e5098e"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795427118615044002,"uuid":"5be47f16-39f8-4c2e-9961-ad59c6eb7661"}